# Vendored dependencies must survive checkout byte-for-byte.
#
# Git's autocrlf rewrites line endings on checkout. For cerebro/web/vendor/* that silently changes
# the files' SHA-256, so tests/test_vendor_integrity.py fails on any fresh clone and — far worse —
# the "unmodified upstream artifact" guarantee in VENDOR.md stops being true the moment someone
# clones the repository. The bytes we verified against npm are not the bytes they would get.
#
# Found by scripts/clean_tree_gate.py on its first run: three integrity tests that pass on every
# developer's desk and fail in a pristine checkout.
cerebro/web/vendor/** -text

# Lockfiles are hash-pinned; a line-ending rewrite invalidates the hashes the same way.
requirements.txt -text
requirements-dev.txt -text
